    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Kyle Tucker** (74.59) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) anchor our lineup, offering the most potent combinations of high-order placement and favorable SP matchups. **Kyle Tucker** thrives against the struggling Gasser, benefiting from a 19% SP skill advantage, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is positioned perfectly in the #2 hole to capitalize on a dynamic platoon edge against Holmes. **Sam Antonacci** also warrants attention; despite a park penalty, his elite xwOBA (0.397) and the #1 lineup spot\u2014combined with wind blowing out\u2014yield an impressive 67.67 score, making him a primary target for stolen base production, which remains our highest priority category.\n\nThe toughest decision on the bench was **Nolan Schanuel** (41.64), who hovered near the marginal threshold but was ultimately pushed out by the higher ceiling of our active starters against weaker arms. While **Nolan Schanuel** receives a boost from hitting 3rd, the high-skill ceiling of Eovaldi suppresses his efficiency enough to justify keeping him stashed to preserve our daily game caps. Meanwhile, we are managing significant volatility elsewhere: **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.73) is a start-by-default despite a daunting matchup against Skenes, where the elite 2.96 xERA forces a massive 19% downgrade to his floor. Conversely, we are avoiding any risk with **Gunnar Henderson**, as his game has been postponed, and we continue to monitor the IL status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** as we look for rotation upgrades. **Liam Hicks** and **Jackson Merrill** remain riskier plays today due to lineup uncertainty and tougher pitching assignments, but their dynamic platoon splits keep them just above our bench threshold.",
